179106	179311	179103	179103	his	208	“ I suppose some of us go on faster than others : and I am sure she is a creature who keeps strong traces of anything that has once impressed her . That little affair of the necklace , and the idea that somebody thought her gambling wrong , had evidently bitten into her . But such impressibility leads both ways : it may drive one to desperation as soon as to anything better . And whatever fascinations Grandcourt may have for capricious tastes — good heavens ! who can believe that he would call out the tender affections in daily companionship ? One might be tempted to horsewhip him for the sake of getting some show of passion into his face and speech . I ’m afraid she married him out of ambition — to escape poverty . But why did she run out of his way at first ? The poverty came after , though . Poor thing ! she may have been urged into it . How can one feel anything else than pity for a young creature like that — full of unused life — ignorantly rash — hanging all her blind expectations on that remnant of a human being . ”
