286832	286933	286817	286817	she	6169	“ I meant never to marry again . I meant to be free and to live for my art . I had parted with you . I had no bonds . For nine years I was a queen . I enjoyed the life I had longed for . But something befell me . It was like a fit of forgetfulness . I began to sing out of tune . They told me of it . Another woman was thrusting herself in my place . I could not endure the prospect of failure and decline . It was horrible to me . ”
